        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.064,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Lines and Angles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.121,
            0.834,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "Justify why the two angles are equal. Is there a way to superimpose and check? Can this superimposition be done by folding?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.188,
            0.834,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "Each of these equal angles formed are called right angles. So, a straight angle contains two **right angles**."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.253,
            0.718,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.664,
            0.833,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "If a straight angle is formed by half of a full turn, how much of a full turn will form a right angle?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.716,
            0.834,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": "Observe that a right angle resembles the shape of an ‘L’. An angle is a right angle only if it is exactly half of a straight angle. Two lines that meet at right angles are called **perpendicular** lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.795,
            0.302,
            0.818
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.825,
            0.833,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "1. How many right angles do the windows of your classroom contain? Do you see other right angles in your classroom?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
